5. Provide a concise, factual answer without explanations or reasoning.
6. Use exact names or dates as provided in the summaries, preserving formatting (e.g., “November 25, 1953” or “24 August 1938”).
7. Avoid adding any information not present in the summaries or conjecture beyond what both summaries confirm.

